
Breaking Cyclic Mapping: Simple Explanation
@Entity
public class Department {

    @Id
    private Integer did;
    private String dname;

    @OneToOne
    @JsonManagedReference  // ← This is the "forward" side
    private Employee employee;

}

@Entity
public class Employee {
    @Id
    private Integer id;
    private String name;

    @OneToOne
    @JoinColumn(name = "D_id")
    @JsonBackReference  // ← This is the "back" side (omitted from JSON)
    private Department dep;

}

or we can used @JsonIgnore

5. Foreign Key Strategies
Strategy 1: Shared Primary Key

java@Entity
@Table(name = "user_account")
public class User {

    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Integer id;

    private String username;

    @OneToOne(cascade = CascadeType.ALL)
    @PrimaryKeyJoinColumn  // Uses same PK as User
    private UserProfile profile;
}

@Entity
@Table(name = "user_profile")
public class UserProfile {
    @Id
    private Integer id;  // Same value as User.id

    private String bio;

    // FK to user_account.id implicit
}
Strategy 2: Foreign Key in Child (Most Common)
